Why the name "PetZonic":

Simple reason — when a customer kind of me, just searching in the browser for a pet shop nearby, whatever keyword they type, the platform's name needed to be right there in that search. "Pet" for the obvious search term, "Zonic" for zone — a complete zone covering everything a pet owner needs. PetZonic.


Why PetZonic — My Story

For the last 5 years, I've been a bird breeder — breeding, buying, and selling birds directly to customers, and also running a shop stocked with a wide variety of breeds.

How it all started:
My own journey began with almost nothing: just ₹350 for a setup and a total initial investment of ₹750. From that humble ₹750 start, over the period, I generated over ₹4 Lakhs+ (₹4L+) in returns (ROI).

The realization — Small Circle vs. India's True Market Cap:
The most eye-opening part? My personal circle was very small — I barely knew 100 people locally. If someone with an initial setup of ₹750 and a network of just 100 local contacts can generate ₹4L+ in revenue, what does the market look like when you unlock all of India? The actual market cap across the country is massive, but it was completely locked inside small, isolated pockets.

The Brokerage Struggle & Precious Time:
Along the way, I didn't just breed; I also acted as a trader and broker, connecting buyers with other breeders. But doing this manually took an immense toll. Coordinating calls, negotiating, confirming stock, and managing logistics consumed countless hours every single day. For a breeder, time is the single most precious resource — time that should be spent caring for the pets, improving breeding lines, and scaling the setup. Manual brokering was inefficient and exhausting.

Early on, my biggest struggle wasn't breeding — it was finding other breeders and building real connections with them to grow into a proper farm. There was no dedicated app, no dedicated social platform for this. I started searching manually, slowly making contact with shop owners, until I got added to a few local groups. That's when I realized: there were already dedicated groups for this — organized by location, running on WhatsApp. Then I found Facebook groups too, and that's when it really opened up — these weren't new sellers, these were people who'd been in the pet market for 10-15 years. Back then, Facebook was their only channel for reaching customers outside their immediate network.

I started joining every group I could find — each district has its own dedicated pet-related group, with a minimum of 25,000 people in it. That's when it hit me: there's a genuinely massive market operating quietly in the background. I built connections across districts, starting with Coimbatore, and began buying and selling across district lines.

The real gap:

Anyone new to this — a customer who doesn't know the space — walks straight into a shop, never to the breeder standing on the same street. They don't know the breeder exists, because breeders operate quietly, off to the side. So new customers blindly pay a much higher price at the shop, when a breeder nearby could have sold them a healthier, better-conditioned pet for far less. Meanwhile, shop owners do know exactly where the breeders are — the information asymmetry only runs one way, and it always costs the customer.

By 2026, most breeders had shifted to promoting their farms through Telegram and Instagram — each one now has a minimum of 10,000 followers and solid reach. But even with that reach, the one thing still missing is a dedicated platform built for this market.

Why PetZonic Came: Taking the Business Model to the Next Level

That is the real reason PetZonic came into existence. We want to take this entire traditional pet business model to the next level — making it digital, organized, and scalable so every single breeder and seller can do significantly more business.

Instead of breeders wasting their precious hours acting as manual brokers or being constrained by a local circle of 100 people, PetZonic gives them:
- Direct digital discovery across all of India, unlocking the true national market size.
- Frictionless, automated trading and listing so their time stays focused on breeding quality pets.
- Fair pricing for customers and maximum margins for breeders by removing unnecessary middlemen.
- The world's first complete, end-to-end pet ecosystem under one roof.

Existing platforms each cover only one slice — only vets, only generic products, or only dog/cat catalogs — leaving all the critical gaps wide open. PetZonic was built to solve the entire journey.

Here's how a customer actually moves through this space, and why PetZonic is built to follow them the whole way:

Buy/sell the pet itself — the entry point, straight from breeder to customer.
Accessories — once they own the pet, they start buying gear.
Preowned gadgets — as they grow more invested but aren't ready for full new-setup spend, preowned is the natural second step.
New or premium/branded setup — customers who want to upgrade invest in a proper new or brand-name setup.
Vet consultation — within a week or two of a new setup, health issues often come up, and most customers don't know who to consult. We provide that.
Pharmacy — medicine follow-through after consultation.
Services (e.g., grooming) — ongoing care needs like grooming are handled here too.
Courses/tutorials — customers who want to go deeper get access to guidance from well-known, credentialed people in the space.
Insurance (optional) — for customers holding large or exotic pets, insurance rounds out the ecosystem.
The whole idea is end-to-end: once a customer enters through any one of these doors, we don't lose them to the next step — the platform grows with them.